  "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
  "instance_name": "racial_justification_of_killing",
  "label": "The act of justifying killing based on racial stereotypes or prejudices",
  "description": "Racial justification of killing refers to the act of justifying killing based on racial stereotypes or prejudices, often by implying that the victims are not human or that their killing is not a serious issue. In the meme, the implication that killing zombies (non-human entities) is not homicide is used to justify racially motivated killing. This requires understanding of the concept of racial justification of killing and its role in promoting harmful ideologies.",
